peak\n50\t      differently.\n51\t  - term: command\n52\t    means: >-\n53\t      One command line a user types to run the greeter, its arguments\n54\t      included. Everything a user sees of the greeter follows from one.\n55\t  - term: exit code\n56\t    means: >-\n57\t      The number the command ends with: 0 when it succeeded, anything\n58\t      else when it did not. Scripts calling the greeter branch on it.\n59\t  - term: standard output\n60\t    means: >-\n61\t      The lines the command prints for its user, its answer and its log\n62\t      records alike. It is the greeter's only visible output.\n63\t\n64\tcatalogue:\n65\t  - template: 'the greeting is configured as \"{greeting}\"'\n66\t    block: given\n67\t    means: >-\n68\t      The project's config file sets the greeting, the word the greeter\n69\t      prints before a name, to the quoted text.\n70\t    terms: [greeting]\n71\t  - template: 'the {actor:role} runs \"{command}\"'\n72\t    block: when\n73\t    means: >-\n74\t      That role runs the quoted command line once, in the project\n75\t      directory, and waits for it to exit.\n76\t    terms: [command]\n77\t  - template: 'the command exits with code {code:number}'\n78\t    block: then\n79\t    means: >-\n80\t      The command that role ran ended with that exit code; 0 means it\n81\t      succeeded.\n82\t    terms: [command, exit code]\n83\t  - template: 'stdout matches {expected:pattern}'\n84\t    block: then\n85\t    means: >-\n86\t      A line the command printed to its standard output matches the\n87\t      pattern, a regular expression: either the answer line the command\n88\t      prints for its user, or a log record's message or fields.\n89\t    terms: [command, standard output]\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5defbcb7-9082-4792-8aac-20f8f03c92f0","uuid":"f1ddaf96-c268-4932-aca7-0e9a454490ff","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:13:18.034Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"{{CWD}}/docs/product/product.yaml","conte